      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), we first observe the pattern and group the terms in pairs:\n\n1. Group the odd-indexed terms: \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\)\n2. Group the even-indexed terms: \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + 25 + 31 + 37 + 43 + 49 + 55\\)\n\nLet's analyze these two series.\n\nConsider the odd-indexed series: \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - 16 + \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\)\n\nNotice that this series is an alternating sum of arithmetic progressions. We can calculate its sum using properties of arithmetic sequences.\n\nFirst, let's derive a formula for the arithmetic series sum in each pair.\n\nThe general form of an arithmetic sequence is:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\nwhere \\(a = 7 - 3 = 4\\) (first term), \\(d = 3\\) (common difference), and \\(n\\) ranges over the terms.\n\nThe sum \\(S\\) of the first \\(N\\) terms in an arithmetic progression is given by:\n\\[ S = \\frac{N}{2} \\cdot (2a + (n-1)d) \\]\n\nNow, we need to determine how many terms are in each series set.\n\nFor the odd-numbered series:\n\\[ a = 7 - 3 = 4 \\]\n\\[ d = 3 \\]\n\nThe first term \\(a = 7\\), last term \\(l = 55\\).\n\nUsing the formula above:\n\nFor the last odd number \\(49\\):\n\\[ 49 = 4 + (n-1) \\times 3 \\]\n\\[ 45 = (n-1) \\times 3 \\]\n\\[ n-1 = 15 \\]\n\\[ n = 16 \\]\n\nSo, the series has 16 terms for the odd-numbered set.\n\nNow, let's find the sum separately for the even-numbered series:\n\\[ 1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + 25 + 31 + 37 + 43 + 49 + 55 \\]\n\nWe observe that each term is of the form:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\nwhere \\(a = 1\\), \\(d = 2\\), and \\( n = 15 \\) gives us these terms.\n\nWe calculate:\n\\[ S_{\\text{even}} = \\frac{15}{2} \\cdot (2 \\cdot 1 + (15-1) \\cdot 2) \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{15}{2} \\cdot (2 + 28) \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{15}{2} \\cdot 30 \\]\n\\[ = 15 \\times 15 \\]\n\\[ = 225 \\]\n\nFinally, we sum both series' outcomes:\n\\[ 15 \\times 16 \\]\n\\[ = 240 \\]\n\nSo, the desired output for the sum given in integer form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{240}\n\\]",
