      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), we first identify the pattern of the sequence. The sequence alternates between adding and subtracting terms, and each term is of the form \\(3n+1\\), where \\(n\\) starts from 0. The terms are \\(1, 4, 7, 10, 13, \\ldots, 49, 52, 55\\) with the last term being 55.\n\nWe can group the terms in pairs:\n\\[\n(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - 16) + (19 - 22 + 25 - 28 + 31 - 34) + \\cdots + (53 - 56 + 59 - 62 + 65 - 68) + 69 + 72 - 75 + 78 - 81 + 84 - 87 + 90 - 93 + 96 - 99 + 102\n\\]\n\nEach pair is of the form \\(3n+1 - (3n)= -2\\) if \\(n\\) is the current index in the sequence. The indices start from 0 and increase by 1 each time. The indices are \\(0, 1, 2, \\ldots, 16\\), which correspond to the terms \\(1, 4, 7, \\ldots, 55\\).\n\nThe number of terms in each pair is 4, and there are 4 pairs plus the last term 55. So, there are \\(4 \\times 4 + 1 = 17\\) terms in the sequence from 1 to 102 in steps of 3.\n\nThe sum of each pair is:\n\\[\n-2\n\\]\n\nSince there are 4 such pairs, the sum of all these pairs is:\n\\[\n4 \\times (-2) = -8\n\\]\n\nAdding the last term 55 gives us the final answer:\n\\[\n-8 + 55 = 47\n\\]\n\nSo the value we need to get is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{47}\n\\]",
